<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia offers navy patrol boats to Philippines.</title>
<headline>Indonesia offers navy patrol boats to Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned shipbuilding company PT PAL said on Wednesday it was exploring the possibility of selling fast naval patrol boats to the Philippines.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, we have offered the Philippines the possibility of buying fast patrol boats from us,&quot; a company official told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We gave a presentation last month in the Philippines on the boat. But this is still at an early stage,&quot; said the official, who declined to be named. He gave no other details.</p>
<p>PT PAL is one of Indonesia's strategic companies headed by Research and Technology Minister Jusuf Habibie.</p>
</text>
